<div id="main-content">


			
				<article id="post-33921" class="post-33921 page type-page status-publish has-post-thumbnail hentry">

				
					<div class="entry-content">
					<div class="et-l et-l--post">
			<div class="et_builder_inner_content et_pb_gutters2">
		<div class="et_pb_section et_pb_section_0 castle_explore_section page_top_section et_pb_with_background et_section_regular">
				
				
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_row et_pb_row_0 et_pb_equal_columns et_pb_gutters1">
				<div class="et_pb_column et_pb_column_4_4 et_pb_column_0 custom_cta_column_image  et_pb_css_mix_blend_mode_passthrough et-last-child">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_0  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h2>Plan your visit to Buonconsiglio Castle</h2></div>
			</div>
			</div>
				
				
				
				
			</div>
<div class="et_pb_row et_pb_row_1">
				<div class="et_pb_column et_pb_column_4_4 et_pb_column_1  et_pb_css_mix_blend_mode_passthrough et-last-child">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_1  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner">
<h3>Practical info</h3>
<p>Buonconsiglio Castle is located at <strong>5, Via Bernardo Cles &ndash; Trento</strong> &ndash; Italy &ndash; <a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/sECtrvRDu3KERyKJ7"><strong>Google Maps.</strong></a><br>The Castle does not have its own <strong>parking</strong> facilities, but paid parking is available nearby at:</p>
<ul>
<li>Buonconsiglio multi-storey car park;</li>
<li>Piazza Fiera underground car park;</li>
<li>Centro Europa underground car park, two levels down.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>HOW TO GET TO TRENTO</strong></p>
<p><strong>By car&nbsp;</strong></p>
<p>The Brenner motorway (A22, exit Trento Nord or Trento Sud), state road 12 of Abetone and Brenner (SS12) from Verona or Bolzano, state road 47 of Valsugana (SS47 Valsugana Superstrada) from Venice, and state road 45bis Gardesana Occidentale (SS45bis) for those coming from Brescia and Lake Garda.</p>
<p><strong>By train&nbsp;</strong></p>
<p>The Brenner line and the Valsugana line from Venice. The train station is located near the historic centre of Trento (Piazza Duomo is just a short walk away). At the station, you can also find the terminus for the Trento-Mal&egrave;-Mezzana local train line coming from Val di Sole and the branch of the Valsugana line which leads to Bassano del Grappa and Venice.</p>
<p><strong>By plane</strong></p>
<p>The nearest airports are: Verona (90 km.), Brescia (165 km.), Venice (155 km.), Treviso (130 km.), Milano (250 km.), Bergamo (200 km.) and Bologna (225 km.).</p>
<p><strong>By bus</strong></p>
<p>Trento is well connected to all towns in the province by an efficient bus service, making it easy to reach any town in Trentino; timetables are available on the <strong><a href="https://www.trentinotrasporti.it/en/">Trentino Trasporti page</a></strong>. Furthermore, there is a direct multi-week connection between Trento and some European cities (Prague, Vienna, Innsbruck, Salzburg, Ceske Budejovice), while, in some periods of the year, the same service is carried out towards some Italian cities. Finally, there is the Flixbus service which can be consulted on the page <strong><a href="https://www.flixbus.ie/coach/trento?_sp=56c4d81e-dbba-43aa-acf5-eb1a5f487650.1733400328752&amp;_spnuid=9b20778c-d3bf-4bbf-9a31-1e06d830558b_1733400328524">dedicated webpage.</a></strong></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
			</div>
<div class="et_pb_button_module_wrapper et_pb_button_0_wrapper  et_pb_module ">
				<a class="et_pb_button et_pb_button_0 et_pb_bg_layout_light" href="https://www.buonconsiglio.it/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/BUONCONSIGLIO_mappa.pdf">DOWNLOAD THE MAP</a>
			</div>
			</div>
				
				
				
				
			</div>
<div class="et_pb_row et_pb_row_2">
				<div class="et_pb_column et_pb_column_4_4 et_pb_column_2  et_pb_css_mix_blend_mode_passthrough et-last-child">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_2  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h3>APP&nbsp;</h3></div>
			</div>
<div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_3  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><p>There is an APP dedicated to visit the <strong>Castello del Buonconsiglio</strong>. The APP is free for Apple / Android devices and it offers four itineraries: a standard tour, one with video descriptions in Italian Sign Language (LIS) with subtitles, one with more detailed audio descriptions for blind or visually impaired visitors, and a family-friendly route featuring animations. To use it, an internet connection is required and it is recommended to enable Bluetooth to enhance the visitor experience. No account is needed. To download the app, access the App Store on your device, search for the app name in the search bar or use<strong><a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=it.amuseapp.buonconsiglio&amp;pcampaignid=web_share&amp;pli=1"> the dedicated link</a></strong>, and select &ldquo;Install.&rdquo; For further details, please visit the <strong><a href="https://www.buonconsiglio.it/en/faq/">FAQ page</a></strong>.</p></div>
			</div>
<div class="et_pb_button_module_wrapper et_pb_button_1_wrapper  et_pb_module ">
				<a class="et_pb_button et_pb_button_1 et_pb_bg_layout_light" href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=it.amuseapp.buonconsiglio&amp;pcampaignid=web_share" target="_blank">DOWNLOAD THE APP</a>
			</div>
			</div>
				
				
				
				
			</div>
<div class="et_pb_row et_pb_row_3">
				<div class="et_pb_column et_pb_column_4_4 et_pb_column_3  et_pb_css_mix_blend_mode_passthrough et-last-child">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_4  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h3>PHYSICAL ACCESSIBILITY</h3></div>
			</div>
<div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_5  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner">
<p>Visiting Buonconsiglio Castle in Trento and all its other sites may pose challenges for anyone with mobility difficulties.</p>
</div>
			</div>
<div class="et_pb_module et_pb_divider et_pb_divider_0 et_pb_divider_position_ et_pb_space"><div class="et_pb_divider_internal"></div></div>
<div class="et_pb_module et_pb_toggle et_pb_toggle_0 et_pb_toggle_item  et_pb_toggle_close">
				
				
				
				
				<h5 class="et_pb_toggle_title">BUONCONSIGLIO</h5>
				<div class="et_pb_toggle_content clearfix">
<p>Buonconsiglio Castle has stairs and other physical barriers and there are no elevators.<br>The garden, library and cafeteria can be accessed by a convenient ramp at the Porta San Martino even in a wheelchair.<br>You can admire the frescoes in the Clesian Refectory via the elevator inside the cafeteria.<br>In any case, it is recommended you contact the Museum (tel. +39 0461 492811 and <strong><a href="mailto:education@buonconsiglio.it">dedicates email address</a></strong>) for more precise information regarding access arrangements.</p>
</div>
			</div>
<div class="et_pb_module et_pb_divider et_pb_divider_1 et_pb_divider_position_ et_pb_space"><div class="et_pb_divider_internal"></div></div>
			</div>
				
				
				
				
			</div>
<div id="orari" class="et_pb_row et_pb_row_4">
				<div class="et_pb_column et_pb_column_4_4 et_pb_column_4  et_pb_css_mix_blend_mode_passthrough et-last-child">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_6  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_text_inner">
<h3>OPENING TIMES</h3>
<ul>
<li>from Thursday 1 January to Thursday 30 April: open from Tuesday to Sunday, 9:30 am &ndash; 5:00 pm:</li>
<li>from Friday 1 May to Sunday 1 November: open from Tuesday to Sunday, 10:00 am &ndash; 6:00 pm;</li>
<li>from Tuesday 2 November to Wednesday 6 January 2027: open from Tuesday to Sunday, 9:30 am &ndash; 5:00 pm.</li>
</ul>
<p>Closed every non-holiday Monday and on 25 December.</p>
<p>Special Openings:</p>
<ul>
<li>1 January 2026 and 2027 (9:30 am &ndash; 5:00 pm);</li>
<li>Monday 5 January; Monday 6 April; Monday 1 June 2026;</li>
<li>every Monday in August 2026;</li>
<li>Monday 7 December 2026; Monday 4 January 2027.</li>
</ul>
<p>For the months of January, February, March, April, November and December, on the third Friday of each month there is an extended opening from 5:30 pm to 9:00 pm.<br>For the months of May, June, July, September and October, on the third Friday of each month there is an extended opening from 6:00 pm to 10:00 pm.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>
<strong>PHOTOGRAPHS</strong> and video recordings for editorial, advertising and commercial use are only permitted with prior authorisation;</li>
<li>
<strong>DOG-FRIENDLY</strong>: all dogs may enter the museum gardens provided they are kept on a leash. Only small-sized dogs are allowed to enter if always carried in arms or in a carrier.</li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Choose the date of your visit to view the opening hours.</strong></p>
</div>
